    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Sorry, I didn't mean to imply anything biased. I just meant I'm worried about missing signs because my textbooks mostly show Type I and II skin. For example, if I'm looking for signs of inflammation or erythema in a patient with Fitzpatrick Type V or VI, what specific visual cues should I be looking for instead of the usual redness? Is it more about hyperpigmentation or changes in texture? I just want to make sure I'm being accurate during exams.",
